Rules:
- Organize ALL incidents by root cause class. Each `### Root Cause:` is a distinct failure
  mechanism. Use semantic similarity to match (e.g., "targetPort mismatch" and "Service port
  misconfiguration" are the same class).
- If matching existing root cause: increment Seen, append reference, add novel symptoms/detection
  signals, update mitigations if the new session provides a better approach.
- If novel: create a new `### Root Cause:` entry with all subheadings.
- SPLITTING: If an entry has 5+ incidents with clearly distinct failure mechanisms, split it
  into separate entries.
- Include causal chains when available. Mark "(validated)" or "(unvalidated)" based on benchmark
  confirmation. Upgrade unvalidated to validated when possible. Skip chains marked "N/A".
- Citations MUST use {% raw %}`{{ref:incidents/FILENAME.md}}`{% endraw %} format exactly.
- MIGRATION: If the prior summary uses the old symptom-first format, restructure into
  root-cause-first format.

ABSTRACTION RULES:
- Root causes, causal chains, detection signals, and mitigations must describe the CLASS of
  misconfiguration, not specific instances. Use generic placeholders (<affected-service>,
  <target-port>) instead of specific names or values.
  GOOD: "A Service's targetPort doesn't match the pod's listening port → Connection refused"
  BAD: "text-service targetPort was 9999 while listening on 9090"
- Output the updated Long-Term Summary text only, with no preamble.
